From: DuskyProjects <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: gl-be9300: retain ramoops reservation

Kakatkar's current board DTS carries the factory-derived Wi-Fi MAC cells
needed by the integrated ath12k work. Retain Perceival's tested 1 MiB
ramoops reservation when that DTS is selected as the canonical board
overlay.

---
 target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5332-gl-be9300.dts | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5332-gl-be9300.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5332-gl-be9300.dts
@@ -40,6 +40,19 @@
 		q6_caldb: q6-caldb@4d500000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x4d500000 0x0 0x500000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Preserve the kernel log across a warm reset. The 1 MiB range
+		 * between q6-caldb and mlo-global-mem is the tested Flint 3
+		 * ramoops area.
+		 */
+		ramoops@4da00000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0x4da00000 0x0 0x100000>;
+			console-size = <0x40000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x20000>;
+		};
+
 		mlo_mem: mlo-global-mem@4db00000 {
